## Verdict: INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE

The validation report and findings have been written to:
- `docs/reports/independent_validation_report_deepseek.md` (316 lines)
- `docs/reports/independent_validation_findings_deepseek.json` (323 lines)

### 14 findings: 3 BLOCKING, 4 MAJOR, 5 MODERATE, 2 MINOR

**BLOCKING findings:**

| ID | Finding |
|----|---------|
| V-001 | The unhedged baseline P&L of -56.20% comes from a synthetic GBM path (seed=42), not the observed Massive spot data. The actual observed buy-and-hold return is **-4.61%**. The report claims "BTC declined 56%" — this is fabricated. |
| V-002 | Unhedged `max_drawdown_pct = 0.0` with `total_pnl_pct = -56.2%` — mathematically impossible. Drawdown is never computed for unhedged. |
| V-003 | The strategy comparison mixes synthetic GBM data (unhedged) with observed Massive data (all other strategies). No meaningful comparison is possible. |

**Key evidence:** Reconstructing the GBM path (seed=42, drift=10%, vol=45%, 1303 days from 2023-01-01) independently confirms the -56.20% result, proving it is purely synthetic. The observed `_spot_data_dump.csv` shows start=$66,771.45, end=$63,694.43 — a **-4.61%** return.

**Additional major findings:** The "$11.34B total premium" for covered call includes intrinsic value from deep-ITM options that must be repaid at settlement (not standalone income). Execution sensitivity has zero results. OOS metrics are all null (only 24 cycles available — insufficient for CSCV requiring ≥100).
